          <groundspeak:finder id="25790230">MaybeSunshine</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP307 Willow Creek [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Caps should all be this easy to find, this legible, and in surroundings this pleasant. Saddened (as usual when I visit here) by how many people disregard signage and carve their initials into the scenery. TFTBC.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="687636859">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-20T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="6252216">hunthikers</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP307 Willow Creek

Hunthikers took a trip E for a change, with the goal to geobike along the 11 Bridges road with the geokids and explore the Drumheller area (a place we have never visited before). The weather was warm and comfortable for biking with no wind to worry about. As a bonus to the caches we found, we were also able to grab a few caps. After exploring the hoodoos and getting the data for the earthcache, we wandered over for the cap which is close to an eroding hole.....

{found}

TFTC&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684672354">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3061435">Iron Phoenix</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP307 - Willow Creek&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Out for another day of capping and caching with OBA, this time we went east!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; This one is going to disappear eventually! There is a gaping hole right beside it and under it! I can see the base of the cap! Be very careful walking up to it!! TFTCap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684654541">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="540154">One Bad Ant</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP307 - Willow Creek - this area is pretty amazing. Of course, we picked the wrong elevation first, after a harrowing scramble down the hillside, we found the cap.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
